  "detail": "With $\\mathcal{C}$, $\\tau$, and $\\tau'$ as in Section \\ref{section-compare}. Assume we are given a subset $\\mathcal{P} \\subset \\text{Arrows}(\\mathcal{C})$ and for every object $X$ of $\\mathcal{C}$ we are given a weak Serre subcategory $\\mathcal{A}'_X \\subset \\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C}_{\\tau'}/X)$. We make the following assumption: given $f : X \\to Y$ in $\\mathcal{P}$ and $Y' \\to Y$ general, then $X \\times_Y Y'$ exists and $X \\times_Y Y' \\to Y'$ is in $\\mathcal{P}$, $f_{\\tau'}^{-1}$ sends $\\mathcal{A}'_Y$ into $\\mathcal{A}'_X$ for any morphism $f : X \\to Y$ of $\\mathcal{C}$, given $X$ in $\\mathcal{C}$ and $\\mathcal{F}'$ in $\\mathcal{A}'_X$, then $\\mathcal{F}'$ satisfies the sheaf condition for $\\tau$-coverings, i.e., $\\mathcal{F}' = \\epsilon_{X, *}\\epsilon_X^{-1}\\mathcal{F}'$, if $f : X \\to Y$ in $\\mathcal{P}$ and $\\mathcal{F}' \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{A}'_X)$, then $R^if_{\\tau', *}\\mathcal{F}' \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{A}'_Y)$ for $i \\geq 0$. if $\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$ is a $\\tau$-covering, then there exist a $\\tau'$-covering $\\{V_j \\to U\\}_{j \\in J}$, a $\\tau$-covering $\\{f_j : W_j \\to V_j\\}$ consisting of a single $f_j \\in \\mathcal{P}$, and a $\\tau'$-covering $\\{W_{jk} \\to W_j\\}_{k \\in K_j}$ such that $\\{W_{jk} \\to U\\}_{j \\in J, k \\in K_j}$ is a refinement of $\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$.",
