  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{C}$ and $\\mathcal{D}$ be sites. Let $u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$ be continuous. Assume furthermore the following: the category $\\mathcal{C}$ has a final object $X$ and $u(X)$ is a final object of $\\mathcal{D}$ , and the category $\\mathcal{C}$ has fibre products and $u$ commutes with them. Then $u$ defines a morphism of sites $\\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{C}$, in other words $u_s$ is exact.",
