  "latex": "\\gamma^p : \\Omega^p_{Z/S} \\to \\mathcal{H}^c_Z(\\Omega^{p + c}_{X/S})",
  "name": "lemma · Gysin maps for closed immersions",
  "en": "lemma-gysin-global",
  "importance": 0.65,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $Z \\to X$ be a closed immersion of finite presentation whose conormal sheaf $\\mathcal{C}_{Z/X}$ is locally free of r…",
  "detail": "Let $X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $Z \\to X$ be a closed immersion of finite presentation whose conormal sheaf $\\mathcal{C}_{Z/X}$ is locally free of rank $c$. Then there is a canonical map $$ \\gamma^p : \\Omega^p_{Z/S} \\to \\mathcal{H}^c_Z(\\Omega^{p + c}_{X/S}) $$ which is locally given by the maps $\\gamma^p_{f_1, \\ldots, f_c}$ of Remark \\ref{remark-gysin-equations}.",
