  "detail": "Let $F : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$ be a functor. Suppose all finite limits exist in $\\mathcal{A}$. We say $F$ is {\\it left exact} if it commutes with all finite limits. Suppose all finite colimits exist in $\\mathcal{A}$. We say $F$ is {\\it right exact} if it commutes with all finite colimits. We say $F$ is {\\it exact} if it is both left and right exact.",
