  "summary": "With notations as above assume that $\\mathcal{F}$ is locally quasi-coherent, and for any morphism $(U, T, \\delta) \\to (U', T', \\delta')$ of $\\text{Cris}(X/S)$ w…",
  "detail": "With notations as above assume that $\\mathcal{F}$ is locally quasi-coherent, and for any morphism $(U, T, \\delta) \\to (U', T', \\delta')$ of $\\text{Cris}(X/S)$ where $f : T \\to T'$ is a closed immersion the map $c_f : f^*\\mathcal{F}_{T'} \\to \\mathcal{F}_T$ is surjective. Then the complex $$ M(0) \\to M(1) \\to M(2) \\to \\ldots $$ computes $R\\Gamma(\\text{Cris}(X/S), \\mathcal{F})$.",
