  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a continuous map. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of sets on $X$ and let $\\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of sets on $Y$.…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a continuous map. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of sets on $X$ and let $\\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of sets on $Y$. An {\\it $f$-map $\\xi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$} is a collection of maps $\\xi_V : \\mathcal{G}(V) \\to \\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}(V))$ indexed by open subsets $V \\subset Y$ such that $$ \\xymatrix{ \\mathcal{G}(V) \\ar[r]_{\\xi_V} \\ar[d]_{\\text{restriction of }\\mathcal{G}} & \\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V) \\ar[d]^{\\text{restriction of }\\mathcal{F}} \\\\ \\mathcal{G}(V') \\ar[r]^{\\xi_{V'}} & \\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V') } $$ commutes for all $V' \\subset V \\subset Y$ open.",
