  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{D}$ be a triangulated category. Let $(K_n, f_n)$ be a system of objects of $\\mathcal{D}$.…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{D}$ be a triangulated category. Let $(K_n, f_n)$ be a system of objects of $\\mathcal{D}$. We say an object $K$ is a {\\it derived colimit}, or a {\\it homotopy colimit} of the system $(K_n)$ if the direct sum $\\bigoplus K_n$ exists and there is a distinguished triangle $$ \\bigoplus K_n \\to \\bigoplus K_n \\to K \\to \\bigoplus K_n[1] $$ where the map $\\bigoplus K_n \\to \\bigoplus K_n$ is given by $1 - f_n$ in degree $n$. If this is the case, then we sometimes indicate this by the notation $K = \\text{hocolim} K_n$.",
