  "detail": "Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module of finite type. Let $x \\in X$ be a point with image $s$ in $S$. A {\\it one step d\\'evissage of $\\mathcal{F}/X/S$ at $x$} is a system $(Z, Y, i, \\pi, \\mathcal{G}, z, y)$, where $(Z, Y, i, \\pi, \\mathcal{G})$ is a one step d\\'evissage of $\\mathcal{F}/X/S$ over $s$ and $\\dim_x(\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F}_s)) = \\dim(\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F}_s))$, $z \\in Z$ is a point with $i(z) = x$ and $\\pi(z) = y$, we have $\\pi^{-1}(\\{y\\}) = \\{z\\}$, the extension $\\kappa(y)/\\kappa(s)$ is purely transcendental.",
