  "summary": "Let $X$ be a scheme. Consider triples $(T, E, m)$ where $T \\subset X$ is a closed subset, $E$ is an object of $D_\\QCoh(\\mathcal{O}_X)$, and $m \\in \\mathbf{Z}$.…",
  "detail": "Let $X$ be a scheme. Consider triples $(T, E, m)$ where $T \\subset X$ is a closed subset, $E$ is an object of $D_\\QCoh(\\mathcal{O}_X)$, and $m \\in \\mathbf{Z}$. We say {\\it approximation holds for the triple} $(T, E, m)$ if there exists a perfect object $P$ of $D(\\mathcal{O}_X)$ supported on $T$ and a map $\\alpha : P \\to E$ which induces isomorphisms $H^i(P) \\to H^i(E)$ for $i > m$ and a surjection $H^m(P) \\to H^m(E)$.",
