  "importance": 0.6,
  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $R \\to S$ be a local map of local rings. Choose separable algebraic closures $R/\\mathfrak m_R \\subset \\kappa_1^{sep}$ and $S/\\mathfrak m_S \\subset \\kappa_2^…",
  "detail": "Let $R \\to S$ be a local map of local rings. Choose separable algebraic closures $R/\\mathfrak m_R \\subset \\kappa_1^{sep}$ and $S/\\mathfrak m_S \\subset \\kappa_2^{sep}$. Let $R \\to R^{sh}$ and $S \\to S^{sh}$ be the corresponding strict henselizations. Given any commutative diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ \\kappa_1^{sep} \\ar[r]_{\\phi} & \\kappa_2^{sep} \\\\ R/\\mathfrak m_R \\ar[r]^{\\varphi} \\ar[u] & S/\\mathfrak m_S \\ar[u] } $$ There exists a unique local ring map $R^{sh} \\to S^{sh}$ fitting into the commutative diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ R^{sh} \\ar[r]_f & S^{sh} \\\\ R \\ar[u] \\ar[r] & S \\ar[u] } $$ and inducing $\\phi$ on the residue fields of $R^{sh}$ and $S^{sh}$.",
