  "name": "lemma · Filtered colimits",
  "en": "lemma-split-into-directed",
  "importance": 0.6,
  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{I}$ be an index category, i.e., a category. Assume for every pair of morphisms $a : w \\to x$ and $b : w \\to y$ in $\\mathcal{I}$ there exist an obj…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{I}$ be an index category, i.e., a category. Assume for every pair of morphisms $a : w \\to x$ and $b : w \\to y$ in $\\mathcal{I}$ there exist an object $z$ and morphisms $c : x \\to z$ and $d : y \\to z$ such that $c \\circ a = d \\circ b$, and for every pair of morphisms $a, b : x \\to y$ there exists a morphism $c : y \\to z$ such that $c \\circ a = c \\circ b$. Then $\\mathcal{I}$ is a (possibly empty) union of disjoint filtered index categories $\\mathcal{I}_j$.",
