  "detail": "Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(A, \\text{d})$ and $(B, \\text{d})$ be differential graded algebras over $R$. Let $N$ be a differential graded $(A, B)$-bimodule. Assume that $N$ defines a compact object of $D(B, \\text{d})$, if $N' \\in D(B, \\text{d})$ and $\\Hom_{D(B, \\text{d})}(N, N'[n]) = 0$ for $n \\in \\mathbf{Z}$, then $N' = 0$, and the map $H^k(A) \\to \\Hom_{D(B, \\text{d})}(N, N[k])$ is an isomorphism for all $k \\in \\mathbf{Z}$. Then $$ - \\otimes_A^\\mathbf{L} N : D(A, \\text{d}) \\to D(B, \\text{d}) $$ gives an $R$-linear equivalence of triangulated categories.",
