  "detail": "Let $(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$ be a ringed space. We are given a collection of opens $\\mathcal{B}$ of $X$, for $U \\in \\mathcal{B}$ an object $K_U$ in $D(\\mathcal{O}_U)$, for $V \\subset U$ with $V, U \\in \\mathcal{B}$ an isomorphism $\\rho^U_V : K_U|_V \\to K_V$ in $D(\\mathcal{O}_V)$, such that whenever we have $W \\subset V \\subset U$ with $U, V, W$ in $\\mathcal{B}$, then $\\rho^U_W = \\rho^V_W \\circ \\rho ^U_V|_W$.",
