  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category with enough injectives. A {\\it resolution functor}\\footnote{This is likely nonstandard terminology.} for $\\mathcal{A}$ …",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category with enough injectives. A {\\it resolution functor}\\footnote{This is likely nonstandard terminology.} for $\\mathcal{A}$ is given by the following data: for all $K^\\bullet \\in \\Ob(K^{+}(\\mathcal{A}))$ a bounded below complex of injectives $j(K^\\bullet)$, and for all $K^\\bullet \\in \\Ob(K^{+}(\\mathcal{A}))$ a quasi-isomorphism $i_{K^\\bullet} : K^\\bullet \\to j(K^\\bullet)$.",
