  "importance": 0.59,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{A}, \\mathcal{B}$ be abelian categories. Let $F = (F^n, \\delta_F)$ be a $\\delta$-functor from $\\mathcal{A}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$.…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{A}, \\mathcal{B}$ be abelian categories. Let $F = (F^n, \\delta_F)$ be a $\\delta$-functor from $\\mathcal{A}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$. We say $F$ is a {\\it universal $\\delta$-functor} if and only if for every $\\delta$-functor $G = (G^n, \\delta_G)$ and any morphism of functors $t : F^0 \\to G^0$ there exists a unique morphism of $\\delta$-functors $\\{t^n\\}_{n \\geq 0} : F \\to G$ such that $t = t^0$.",
