  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $x \\in X$. We say that $f$ is {\\it Koszul at $x$} if $f$ is of finite type at $x$ and there exists an open neigh…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $x \\in X$. We say that $f$ is {\\it Koszul at $x$} if $f$ is of finite type at $x$ and there exists an open neighbourhood and a factorization of $f|_U$ as $\\pi \\circ i$ where $i : U \\to P$ is a Koszul-regular immersion and $\\pi : P \\to S$ is smooth. We say $f$ is a {\\it Koszul morphism}, or that $f$ is a {\\it local complete intersection morphism} if $f$ is Koszul at every point.",
