  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. We say that $f$ is {\\it unramified at $x \\in X$} if there exists an affine open neighbourhood $\\Spec(A) = U \\subset …",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. We say that $f$ is {\\it unramified at $x \\in X$} if there exists an affine open neighbourhood $\\Spec(A) = U \\subset X$ of $x$ and affine open $\\Spec(R) = V \\subset S$ with $f(U) \\subset V$ such that the induced ring map $R \\to A$ is unramified. We say that $f$ is {\\it G-unramified at $x \\in X$} if there exists an affine open neighbourhood $\\Spec(A) = U \\subset X$ of $x$ and affine open $\\Spec(R) = V \\subset S$ with $f(U) \\subset V$ such that the induced ring map $R \\to A$ is G-unramified. We say that $f$ is {\\it unramified} if it is unramified at every point of $X$. We say that $f$ is {\\it G-unramified} if it is G-unramified at every point of $X$.",
