  "summary": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be integral schemes. Let $f : X \\to Y$ be locally of finite type and dominant.…",
  "detail": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be integral schemes. Let $f : X \\to Y$ be locally of finite type and dominant. Assume $[R(X) : R(Y)] < \\infty$, or any other of the equivalent conditions (1) -- (4) of Lemma \\ref{lemma-finite-degree}. Then the positive integer $$ \\deg(X/Y) = [R(X) : R(Y)] $$ is called the {\\it degree of $X$ over $Y$}.",
