  "summary": "Let $f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. We say $f$ satisfies the {\\it existence part of the valuative criterion} if for every d…",
  "detail": "Let $f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. We say $f$ satisfies the {\\it existence part of the valuative criterion} if for every diagram (\\ref{equation-diagram}) and $\\gamma$ as in Definition \\ref{definition-fill-in-diagram} there exists an extension $K'/K$ of fields, a valuation ring $A' \\subset K'$ dominating $A$ such that the category of dotted arrows for the outer rectangle of the diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ \\Spec(K') \\ar[r] \\ar@/^2em/[rr]_{x'} \\ar[d]_{j'} & \\Spec(K) \\ar[d]_j \\ar[r]_-x & \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^f \\\\ \\Spec(A') \\ar[r] \\ar@/_2em/[rr]^{y'} & \\Spec(A) \\ar[r]^-y & \\mathcal{Y} } $$ with induced $2$-arrow $\\gamma' : y' \\circ j' \\to f \\circ x'$ is nonempty.",
