  "url": "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/065V",
  "env": "lemma",
  "latex": "I/I^2 \\to J/J^2 \\to \\Omega_{B/A} \\otimes_B B/J \\to 0",
  "name": "lemma · The naive cotangent complex",
  "en": "lemma-application-NL",
  "importance": 0.58,
  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $A \\to B \\to C$ be ring maps. Assume $A \\to C$ is surjective (so also $B \\to C$ is). Denote $I = \\Ker(A \\to C)$ and $J = \\Ker(B \\to C)$.…",
  "detail": "Let $A \\to B \\to C$ be ring maps. Assume $A \\to C$ is surjective (so also $B \\to C$ is). Denote $I = \\Ker(A \\to C)$ and $J = \\Ker(B \\to C)$. Then the sequence $$ I/I^2 \\to J/J^2 \\to \\Omega_{B/A} \\otimes_B B/J \\to 0 $$ is exact.",
