  "detail": "Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a $1$-dimensional algebraic $k$-scheme. Let $x \\in X$ be a closed point. The following are equivalent $x$ is a node, $k \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is as in Lemma \\ref{lemma-nodal-algebraic}, any $\\overline{x} \\in X_{\\overline{k}}$ mapping to $x$ defines a nodal singularity, $\\kappa(x)/k$ is separable, $\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is reduced, and the first Fitting ideal of $\\Omega_{X/k}$ generates $\\mathfrak m_x$ in $\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$, $\\kappa(x)/k$ is separable, $\\text{depth}(\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}) = 1$, and the first Fitting ideal of $\\Omega_{X/k}$ generates $\\mathfrak m_x$ in $\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$, $\\kappa(x)/k$ is separable and $\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is reduced, has $\\delta$-invariant $1$, and has $2$ geometric branches.",
