  "en": "lemma-products",
  "importance": 0.58,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category with exact countable products. Then $D(\\mathcal{A})$ has countable products, countable products $\\prod K_i$ in $D(\\math…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category with exact countable products. Then $D(\\mathcal{A})$ has countable products, countable products $\\prod K_i$ in $D(\\mathcal{A})$ are obtained by taking termwise products of any complexes representing the $K_i$, and $H^p(\\prod K_i) = \\prod H^p(K_i)$.",
