  "env": "lemma",
  "latex": "\\Hom_{\\text{Mod}_{(A, d)}}(M', \\Hom(M, N^\\bullet)) = \\Hom_{\\text{Comp}(R)}(M' \\otimes_A M, N^\\bullet)",
  "name": "lemma · Hom complexes and differential graded modules",
  "en": "lemma-characterize-hom",
  "importance": 0.58,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(A, \\text{d})$ be a differential graded $R$-algebra. Let $M'$ be a right differential graded $A$-module and let $M$ be a left differenti…",
  "detail": "Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(A, \\text{d})$ be a differential graded $R$-algebra. Let $M'$ be a right differential graded $A$-module and let $M$ be a left differential graded $A$-module. Let $N^\\bullet$ be a complex of $R$-modules. Then we have $$ \\Hom_{\\text{Mod}_{(A, d)}}(M', \\Hom(M, N^\\bullet)) = \\Hom_{\\text{Comp}(R)}(M' \\otimes_A M, N^\\bullet) $$ where $M \\otimes_A M$ is viewed as a complex of $R$-modules as in Section \\ref{section-tensor-product}.",
