  "detail": "Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(A, \\text{d})$ and $(B, \\text{d})$ be differential graded $R$-algebras. Let $N$ be a differential graded $(A, B)$-bimodule. Then the functor $$ - \\otimes_A^\\mathbf{L} N : D(A, \\text{d}) \\longrightarrow D(B, \\text{d}) $$ of Lemma \\ref{lemma-derived-bc} is a left adjoint to the functor $$ R\\Hom(N, -) : D(B, \\text{d}) \\longrightarrow D(A, \\text{d}) $$ of Lemma \\ref{lemma-derived-restriction}.",
