  "summary": "In Situation \\ref{situation-shriek} let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of $\\textit{FTS}_S$. Assume $f$ is perfect (e.g., flat).…",
  "detail": "In Situation \\ref{situation-shriek} let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of $\\textit{FTS}_S$. Assume $f$ is perfect (e.g., flat). Then [(a)] $f^!\\mathcal{O}_Y$ is in $D_{\\textit{Coh}}^b(\\mathcal{O}_X)$, [(b)] $f^!\\mathcal{O}_Y$ has finite tor dimension in $D(f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y)$, [(c)] $\\mathcal{O}_X \\to R\\SheafHom_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(f^!\\mathcal{O}_Y, f^!\\mathcal{O}_Y)$ is an isomorphism, [(d)] $f^!$ maps $D_{\\textit{Coh}}^b(\\mathcal{O}_Y)$ into $D_{\\textit{Coh}}^b(\\mathcal{O}_X)$, [(e)] the map $\\mu_{f, K} : Lf^*K \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_X}^\\mathbf{L} f^!\\mathcal{O}_Y \\to f^!K$ of Lemma \\ref{lemma-map-pullback-to-shriek-well-defined} is an isomorphism for all $K \\in D_\\QCoh^+(\\mathcal{O}_Y)$.",
