  "summary": "Let $R \\to S$ be a ring map. Let $N$ be a $S$-module. Assume $R$ is a local ring with maximal ideal $\\mathfrak m$, $\\overline{S} = S/\\mathfrak m S$ is Noetheria…",
  "detail": "Let $R \\to S$ be a ring map. Let $N$ be a $S$-module. Assume $R$ is a local ring with maximal ideal $\\mathfrak m$, $\\overline{S} = S/\\mathfrak m S$ is Noetherian, and $\\overline{N} = N/\\mathfrak m_R N$ is a finite $\\overline{S}$-module. Let $\\Sigma \\subset S$ be the multiplicative subset of elements which are not a zerodivisor on $\\overline{N}$. Then $\\Sigma^{-1}S$ is a semi-local ring whose spectrum consists of primes $\\mathfrak q \\subset S$ contained in an element of $\\text{Ass}_S(\\overline{N})$. Moreover, any maximal ideal of $\\Sigma^{-1}S$ corresponds to an associated prime of $\\overline{N}$ over $\\overline{S}$.",
