  "name": "lemma · Cohomological delta-functors",
  "en": "lemma-efface-implies-universal",
  "importance": 0.58,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{A}, \\mathcal{B}$ be abelian categories. Let $F = (F^n, \\delta_F)$ be a $\\delta$-functor from $\\mathcal{A}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$.…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{A}, \\mathcal{B}$ be abelian categories. Let $F = (F^n, \\delta_F)$ be a $\\delta$-functor from $\\mathcal{A}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$. Suppose that for every $n > 0$ and any $A \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{A})$ there exists an injective morphism $u : A \\to B$ (depending on $A$ and $n$) such that $F^n(u) : F^n(A) \\to F^n(B)$ is zero. Then $F$ is a universal $\\delta$-functor.",
