  "detail": "Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\\mathcal{O}_1 \\to \\mathcal{O}_2$ be a map of sheaves of rings on $X$. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_2$-modules. Let $k \\geq 0$. There exists a sheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_2$-modules $\\mathcal{P}^k_{\\mathcal{O}_2/\\mathcal{O}_1}(\\mathcal{F})$ and a canonical isomorphism $$ \\text{Diff}^k_{\\mathcal{O}_2/\\mathcal{O}_1}(\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{G}) = \\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_2}( \\mathcal{P}^k_{\\mathcal{O}_2/\\mathcal{O}_1}(\\mathcal{F}), \\mathcal{G}) $$ functorial in the $\\mathcal{O}_2$-module $\\mathcal{G}$.",
