  "summary": "Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X, Y \\subset S$ be closed subschemes. Let $X \\cup Y$ be the scheme theoretic union of $X$ and $Y$.…",
  "detail": "Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X, Y \\subset S$ be closed subschemes. Let $X \\cup Y$ be the scheme theoretic union of $X$ and $Y$. Let $X \\cap Y$ be the scheme theoretic intersection of $X$ and $Y$. Then $X \\to X \\cup Y$ and $Y \\to X \\cup Y$ are closed immersions, there is a short exact sequence $$ 0 \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X \\cup Y} \\to \\mathcal{O}_X \\times \\mathcal{O}_Y \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X \\cap Y} \\to 0 $$ of $\\mathcal{O}_S$-modules, and the diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ X \\cap Y \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\ar[d] \\\\ Y \\ar[r] & X \\cup Y } $$ is cocartesian in the category of schemes, i.e., $X \\cup Y = X \\amalg_{X \\cap Y} Y$.",
