  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "With notations $G$, $G\\textit{-Sets}_\\alpha$, $\\text{size}$, and $Bound$ as above. Let $S_0$ be a set of $G$-sets.…",
  "detail": "With notations $G$, $G\\textit{-Sets}_\\alpha$, $\\text{size}$, and $Bound$ as above. Let $S_0$ be a set of $G$-sets. There exists a limit ordinal $\\alpha$ with the following properties: We have $S_0 \\cup \\{{}_GG\\} \\subset \\Ob(G\\textit{-Sets}_\\alpha)$. For any $S \\in \\Ob(G\\textit{-Sets}_\\alpha)$ and any $G$-set $T$ with $\\text{size}(T) \\leq Bound(\\text{size}(S))$, there exists an $S' \\in \\Ob(G\\textit{-Sets}_\\alpha)$ that is isomorphic to $T$. For any countable index category $\\mathcal{I}$ and any functor $F : \\mathcal{I} \\to G\\textit{-Sets}_\\alpha$, the limit $\\lim_\\mathcal{I} F$ and colimit $\\colim_\\mathcal{I} F$ exist in $G\\textit{-Sets}_\\alpha$ and are the same as in $G\\textit{-Sets}$.",
