  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a site. If $s : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$ is a morphism of sheaves on $\\mathcal{C}$ then there exists a natural commutative diagram of morphisms of topoi $$ \\xymatrix{ \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/\\mathcal{G} \\ar[rd]_{j_\\mathcal{G}} \\ar[rr]_j & & \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/\\mathcal{F} \\ar[ld]^{j_\\mathcal{F}} \\\\ & \\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) & } $$ where $j = j_{\\mathcal{G}/\\mathcal{F}}$ is the localization of the topos $\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/\\mathcal{F}$ at the object $\\mathcal{G}/\\mathcal{F}$. In particular we have $$ j^{-1}(\\mathcal{H} \\to \\mathcal{F}) = (\\mathcal{H} \\times_\\mathcal{F} \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{G}) $$ and $$ j_!(\\mathcal{E} \\xrightarrow{e} \\mathcal{G}) = (\\mathcal{E} \\xrightarrow{s \\circ e} \\mathcal{F}). $$",
