  "summary": "Let $Y$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $x$ be a point of $X$.…",
  "detail": "Let $Y$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $x$ be a point of $X$. The following are equivalent $f$ is unramified at $x$, the stalk $\\Omega_{X/Y, x}$ of the module of relative differentials at $x$ is trivial, there exist open neighbourhoods $U$ of $x$ and $V$ of $f(x)$, and a commutative diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ U \\ar[rr]_i \\ar[rd] & & \\mathbf{A}^n_V \\ar[ld] \\\\ & V } $$ where $i$ is a closed immersion defined by a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals $\\mathcal{I}$ such that the differentials $\\text{d}g$ for $g \\in \\mathcal{I}_{i(x)}$ generate $\\Omega_{\\mathbf{A}^n_V/V, i(x)}$, and the diagonal $\\Delta_{X/Y} : X \\to X \\times_Y X$ is a local isomorphism at $x$.",
