  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $\\varphi : R \\to S$ be a ring map and let $M$ be an $S$-module. A {\\it derivation}, or more precisely an {\\it $R$-derivation} into $M$ is a map $D : S \\to M…",
  "detail": "Let $\\varphi : R \\to S$ be a ring map and let $M$ be an $S$-module. A {\\it derivation}, or more precisely an {\\it $R$-derivation} into $M$ is a map $D : S \\to M$ which is additive, annihilates elements of $\\varphi(R)$, and satisfies the {\\it Leibniz rule}: $D(ab) = aD(b) + bD(a)$.",
