  "latex": "\\overline{f'}(a_0) \\not = 0",
  "name": "definition · Henselian local rings",
  "en": "definition-henselian",
  "importance": 0.55,
  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $(R, \\mathfrak m, \\kappa)$ be a local ring. We say $R$ is {\\it henselian} if for every monic $f \\in R[T]$ and every root $a_0 \\in \\kappa$ of $\\overline{f}$ …",
  "detail": "Let $(R, \\mathfrak m, \\kappa)$ be a local ring. We say $R$ is {\\it henselian} if for every monic $f \\in R[T]$ and every root $a_0 \\in \\kappa$ of $\\overline{f}$ such that $\\overline{f'}(a_0) \\not = 0$ there exists an $a \\in R$ such that $f(a) = 0$ and $a_0 = \\overline{a}$. We say $R$ is {\\it strictly henselian} if $R$ is henselian and its residue field is separably algebraically closed.",
