  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Suppose that $F : \\mathcal{C}^{opp} \\to \\textit{Cat}$ is a functor to the $2$-category of categories.…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Suppose that $F : \\mathcal{C}^{opp} \\to \\textit{Cat}$ is a functor to the $2$-category of categories. We will write $p_F : \\mathcal{S}_F \\to \\mathcal{C}$ for the fibred category constructed in Example \\ref{example-functor-categories}. A {\\it split fibred category} is a fibred category isomorphic (!) over $\\mathcal{C}$ to one of these categories {\\it $\\mathcal{S}_F$}.",
