  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "In Situation \\ref{situation-F-crystal} an {\\it $F$-crystal on $X/S$ (relative to $\\sigma$)} is a pair $(\\mathcal{E}, F_\\mathcal{E})$ given by a crystal in finit…",
  "detail": "In Situation \\ref{situation-F-crystal} an {\\it $F$-crystal on $X/S$ (relative to $\\sigma$)} is a pair $(\\mathcal{E}, F_\\mathcal{E})$ given by a crystal in finite locally free $\\mathcal{O}_{X/S}$-modules $\\mathcal{E}$ together with a map $$ F_\\mathcal{E} : (F_X)_{\\text{cris}}^*\\mathcal{E} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{E} $$ An $F$-crystal is called {\\it nondegenerate} if there exists an integer $i \\geq 0$ a map $V : \\mathcal{E} \\to (F_X)_{\\text{cris}}^*\\mathcal{E}$ such that $V \\circ F_{\\mathcal{E}} = p^i \\text{id}$.",
