  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{D}$ be a pre-triangulated category. Let $\\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. An additive functor $H : \\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{A}$ is called {\\it homological} if for every distinguished triangle $(X, Y, Z, f, g, h)$ the sequence $$ H(X) \\to H(Y) \\to H(Z) $$ is exact in the abelian category $\\mathcal{A}$. An additive functor $H : \\mathcal{D}^{opp} \\to \\mathcal{A}$ is called {\\it cohomological} if the corresponding functor $\\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{A}^{opp}$ is homological.",
