  "importance": 0.55,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "In Situation \\ref{situation-classical}. The {\\it right derived functors of $F$} are the partial functors $RF$ associated to cases (1) and (2) of Situation \\ref{…",
  "detail": "In Situation \\ref{situation-classical}. The {\\it right derived functors of $F$} are the partial functors $RF$ associated to cases (1) and (2) of Situation \\ref{situation-classical}. The {\\it left derived functors of $F$} are the partial functors $LF$ associated to cases (3) and (4) of Situation \\ref{situation-classical}. An object $A$ of $\\mathcal{A}$ is said to be {\\it right acyclic for $F$}, or {\\it acyclic for $RF$} if $A[0]$ computes $RF$. An object $A$ of $\\mathcal{A}$ is said to be {\\it left acyclic for $F$}, or {\\it acyclic for $LF$} if $A[0]$ computes $LF$.",
