  "tag": "02KO",
  "url": "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02KO",
  "env": "definition",
  "latex": "f \\text{ has }\\mathcal{P} \\Leftrightarrow \\text{each }Y_i \\times_Y X \\to Y_i\\text{ has }\\mathcal{P}.",
  "name": "definition · Properties of morphisms local on the target",
  "en": "definition-property-morphisms-local",
  "importance": 0.55,
  "family": "birational",
  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{P}$ be a property of morphisms of schemes over a base. Let $\\tau \\in \\{fpqc, fppf, syntomic, smooth, \\etale, Zariski\\}$.…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{P}$ be a property of morphisms of schemes over a base. Let $\\tau \\in \\{fpqc, fppf, syntomic, smooth, \\etale, Zariski\\}$. We say $\\mathcal{P}$ is {\\it $\\tau$ local on the base}, or {\\it $\\tau$ local on the target}, or {\\it local on the base for the $\\tau$-topology} if for any $\\tau$-covering $\\{Y_i \\to Y\\}_{i \\in I}$ (see Topologies, Section \\ref{topologies-section-procedure}) and any morphism of schemes $f : X \\to Y$ over $S$ we have $$ f \\text{ has }\\mathcal{P} \\Leftrightarrow \\text{each }Y_i \\times_Y X \\to Y_i\\text{ has }\\mathcal{P}. $$",
  "source": "Stacks Project, definition 02KO（descent.tex · Properties of morphisms local on the target）"
