  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $(A, \\text{d})$ be a differential graded algebra. A homomorphism $K \\to L$ of differential graded $A$-modules is an {\\it admissible monomorphism} if there e…",
  "detail": "Let $(A, \\text{d})$ be a differential graded algebra. A homomorphism $K \\to L$ of differential graded $A$-modules is an {\\it admissible monomorphism} if there exists a graded $A$-module map $L \\to K$ which is left inverse to $K \\to L$. A homomorphism $L \\to M$ of differential graded $A$-modules is an {\\it admissible epimorphism} if there exists a graded $A$-module map $M \\to L$ which is right inverse to $L \\to M$. A short exact sequence $0 \\to K \\to L \\to M \\to 0$ of differential graded $A$-modules is an {\\it admissible short exact sequence} if it is split as a sequence of graded $A$-modules.",
  "source": "Stacks Project, definition 09JT（dga.tex · Admissible short exact sequences）"
