  "importance": 0.55,
  "family": "birational",
  "summary": "(See Morphisms, Definition \\ref{morphisms-definition-etale}.) Let $Y$ be a locally Noetherian scheme.…",
  "detail": "(See Morphisms, Definition \\ref{morphisms-definition-etale}.) Let $Y$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $x \\in X$. We say $f$ is {\\it \\'etale at $x \\in X$} if $\\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is an \\'etale homomorphism of local rings. The morphism is said to be {\\it \\'etale} if it is \\'etale at all its points.",
