  "family": "map",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. We say $f$ is {\\it formally unramified} if given any solid commutative diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ X \\ar[d]_f & T \\ar[d]^i…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. We say $f$ is {\\it formally unramified} if given any solid commutative diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ X \\ar[d]_f & T \\ar[d]^i \\ar[l] \\\\ S & T' \\ar[l] \\ar@{-->}[lu] } $$ where $T \\subset T'$ is a first order thickening of affine schemes over $S$ there exists at most one dotted arrow making the diagram commute.",
