  "importance": 0.55,
  "family": "map",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume that all the fibres $X_y$ are locally Noetherian schemes. Let $x \\in X$, and $y = f(x)$.…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume that all the fibres $X_y$ are locally Noetherian schemes. Let $x \\in X$, and $y = f(x)$. We say that $f$ is {\\it Cohen-Macaulay at $x$} if $f$ is flat at $x$, and the local ring of the scheme $X_y$ at $x$ is Cohen-Macaulay. We say $f$ is a {\\it Cohen-Macaulay morphism} if $f$ is Cohen-Macaulay at every point of $X$.",
