  "importance": 0.55,
  "family": "map",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. We say $f$ is {\\it submersive}\\footnote{This is very different from the notion of a submersion of differential manif…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. We say $f$ is {\\it submersive}\\footnote{This is very different from the notion of a submersion of differential manifolds.} if the continuous map of underlying topological spaces is submersive, see Topology, Definition \\ref{topology-definition-submersive}. We say $f$ is {\\it universally submersive} if for every morphism of schemes $Y' \\to Y$ the base change $Y' \\times_Y X \\to Y'$ is submersive.",
