  "latex": "\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I} \\in \\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{C})",
  "name": "definition · Sheaves",
  "en": "definition-sheaf-sets",
  "importance": 0.55,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a site, and let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf of sets on $\\mathcal{C}$.…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a site, and let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf of sets on $\\mathcal{C}$. We say $\\mathcal{F}$ is a {\\it sheaf} if for every covering $\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I} \\in \\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{C})$ the diagram \\begin{equation} \\xymatrix{ \\mathcal{F}(U) \\ar[r] & \\prod\\nolimits_{i\\in I} \\mathcal{F}(U_i) \\ar@<1ex>[r]^-{\\text{pr}_0^*} \\ar@<-1ex>[r]_-{\\text{pr}_1^*} & \\prod\\nolimits_{(i_0, i_1) \\in I \\times I} \\mathcal{F}(U_{i_0} \\times_U U_{i_1}) } \\end{equation} represents the first arrow as the equalizer of $\\text{pr}_0^*$ and $\\text{pr}_1^*$.",
  "source": "Stacks Project, definition 00VM（sites.tex · Sheaves）"
