  "detail": "Notation $U \\to S$, $G$, $R$ as in Lemma \\ref{lemma-quotient}. If the action of $G$ on $U$ satisfies $(*)$ we say $G$ {\\it acts freely} on the scheme $U$. In this case the algebraic space $U/R$ is denoted $U/G$ and is called the {\\it quotient of $U$ by $G$}.",
