  "env": "definition",
  "latex": "Z \\subset |\\mathcal{X}|",
  "name": "definition · Reduced algebraic stacks",
  "en": "definition-reduced-induced-stack",
  "importance": 0.55,
  "family": "modern",
  "summary": "Let $\\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack. Let $Z \\subset |\\mathcal{X}|$ be a closed subset.…",
  "detail": "Let $\\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack. Let $Z \\subset |\\mathcal{X}|$ be a closed subset. An {\\it algebraic stack structure on $Z$} is given by a closed substack $\\mathcal{Z}$ of $\\mathcal{X}$ with $|\\mathcal{Z}|$ equal to $Z$. The {\\it reduced induced algebraic stack structure} on $Z$ is the one constructed in Lemma \\ref{lemma-reduced-closed-substack}. The {\\it reduction $\\mathcal{X}_{red}$ of $\\mathcal{X}$} is the reduced induced algebraic stack structure on $|\\mathcal{X}|$.",
