  "summary": "Let $p : \\mathcal{X} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$ be a category fibred in groupoids. Let $\\mathcal{O}$ be the sheaf of rings on $\\mathcal{X}_{affine}$ introduced in Sec…",
  "detail": "Let $p : \\mathcal{X} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$ be a category fibred in groupoids. Let $\\mathcal{O}$ be the sheaf of rings on $\\mathcal{X}_{affine}$ introduced in Section \\ref{section-alternative}. We define the {\\it triangulated category of quasi-coherent objects in the derived category} by the formula $$ \\mathit{QC}(\\mathcal{X}) = \\mathit{QC}(\\mathcal{X}_{affine}, \\mathcal{O}) $$ where the right hand side is as defined in Cohomology on Sites, Definition \\ref{sites-cohomology-definition-cartesian}.",
