  "importance": 0.54,
  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $K$ be a field. Let $n, m \\in \\mathbf{N}$ and $a_0, \\ldots, a_{n - 1}, b_0, \\ldots, b_{m - 1} \\in K$.…",
  "detail": "Let $K$ be a field. Let $n, m \\in \\mathbf{N}$ and $a_0, \\ldots, a_{n - 1}, b_0, \\ldots, b_{m - 1} \\in K$. If the polynomial $x^n + a_{n - 1}x^{n - 1} + \\ldots + a_0$ divides the polynomial $x^m + b_{m - 1} x^{m - 1} + \\ldots + b_0$ in $K[x]$ then $a_0, \\ldots, a_{n - 1}$ are integral over any subring $R_0$ of $K$ containing the elements $b_0, \\ldots, b_{m - 1}$, and each $a_i$ lies in $\\sqrt{(b_0, \\ldots, b_{m-1})R}$ for any subring $R \\subset K$ containing the elements $a_0, \\ldots, a_{n - 1}, b_0, \\ldots, b_{m - 1}$.",
