  "detail": "Let $R \\to S$ be a ring map. Let $N$ be an $S$-module. Let $A$, $A'$, $A_{fin}$, $B$, and $B_{fin}$ be the subsets of $\\Spec(S)$ introduced above. We always have $A = A'$. We always have $A_{fin} \\subset A$, $B_{fin} \\subset B$, $A_{fin} \\subset A'_{fin} \\subset B_{fin}$ and $A \\subset B$. If $S$ is Noetherian, then $A = A_{fin}$ and $B = B_{fin}$. If $N$ is flat over $R$, then $A = A_{fin} = A'_{fin}$ and $B = B_{fin}$. If $R$ is Noetherian and $N$ is flat over $R$, then all of the sets are equal, i.e., $A = A' = A_{fin} = A'_{fin} = B = B_{fin}$.",
