  "detail": "Let $M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$ be a diagram. Write $I = \\Ob(\\mathcal{I})$ and $A = \\text{Arrows}(\\mathcal{I})$. Denote $s, t : A \\to I$ the source and target maps. Suppose that $\\prod_{i \\in I} M_i$ and $\\prod_{a \\in A} M_{t(a)}$ exist. Suppose that the equalizer of $$ \\xymatrix{ \\prod_{i \\in I} M_i \\ar@<1ex>[r]^\\phi \\ar@<-1ex>[r]_\\psi & \\prod_{a \\in A} M_{t(a)} } $$ exists, where the morphisms are determined by their components as follows: $p_a \\circ \\psi = M(a) \\circ p_{s(a)}$ and $p_a \\circ \\phi = p_{t(a)}$. Then this equalizer is the limit of the diagram.",
