  "detail": "Let $M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$ be a diagram. Write $I = \\Ob(\\mathcal{I})$ and $A = \\text{Arrows}(\\mathcal{I})$. Denote $s, t : A \\to I$ the source and target maps. Suppose that $\\coprod_{i \\in I} M_i$ and $\\coprod_{a \\in A} M_{s(a)}$ exist. Suppose that the coequalizer of $$ \\xymatrix{ \\coprod_{a \\in A} M_{s(a)} \\ar@<1ex>[r]^\\phi \\ar@<-1ex>[r]_\\psi & \\coprod_{i \\in I} M_i } $$ exists, where the morphisms are determined by their components as follows: The component $M_{s(a)}$ maps via $\\psi$ to the component $M_{t(a)}$ via the morphism $M(a)$. The component $M_{s(a)}$ maps via $\\phi$ to the component $M_{s(a)}$ by the identity morphism. Then this coequalizer is the colimit of the diagram.",
