  "detail": "Let $(S, \\delta)$ be as in Situation \\ref{situation-setup}. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $Z \\to X$ be a closed immersion. Let $$ E_1 \\to E_2 \\to E_3 \\to E_1[1] $$ be a distinguished triangle of perfect objects in $D(\\mathcal{O}_X)$. Assume the restrictions $E_1|_{X \\setminus Z}$ and $E_3|_{X \\setminus Z}$ are zero, and at least one of the following is true: (a) $X$ is quasi-compact, (b) $X$ has quasi-compact irreducible components, (c) $E_3 \\to E_1[1]$ can be represented by a map of locally bounded complexes of finite locally free $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules, or (d) there exists an envelope $f : Y \\to X$ such that $Lf^*E_3 \\to Lf^*E_1[1]$ can be represented by a map of locally bounded complexes of finite locally free $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-modules. Then we have $$ P_p(Z \\to X, E_2) = P_p(Z \\to X, E_1) + P_p(Z \\to X, E_3) $$ for all $p \\in \\mathbf{Z}$ and consequently $ch(Z \\to X, E_2) = ch(Z \\to X, E_1) + ch(Z \\to X, E_3)$.",
