  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be an $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module. Let $\\mathcal{E}$ be an $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-module.…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be an $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module. Let $\\mathcal{E}$ be an $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-module. Assume $\\mathcal{E}$ is finite locally free on $Y$, see Modules, Definition \\ref{modules-definition-locally-free}. Then there exist isomorphisms $$ \\mathcal{E} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_Y} R^qf_*\\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow R^qf_*(f^*\\mathcal{E} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_X} \\mathcal{F}) $$ for all $q \\geq 0$. In fact there exists an isomorphism $$ \\mathcal{E} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_Y} Rf_*\\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow Rf_*(f^*\\mathcal{E} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_X} \\mathcal{F}) $$ in $D^{+}(Y)$ functorial in $\\mathcal{F}$.",
