  "env": "lemma",
  "latex": "\\mathcal{I}|_U = \\mathcal{O}_U \\cdot f",
  "name": "lemma · An operator introduced by Berthelot and Ogus",
  "en": "lemma-invertible-ideal-sheaf",
  "importance": 0.54,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$ be a ringed space. Let $\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_X$ be a sheaf of ideals.…",
  "detail": "Let $(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$ be a ringed space. Let $\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_X$ be a sheaf of ideals. Consider the following two conditions for every $x \\in X$ there exists an open neighbourhood $U \\subset X$ of $x$ and $f \\in \\mathcal{I}(U)$ such that $\\mathcal{I}|_U = \\mathcal{O}_U \\cdot f$ and $f : \\mathcal{O}_U \\to \\mathcal{O}_U$ is injective, and $\\mathcal{I}$ is invertible as an $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module. Then (1) implies (2) and the converse is true if all stalks $\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ of the structure sheaf are local rings.",
