  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $(A, I, \\gamma)$ be a divided power ring. Let $A \\to B$ be a ring map. Let $J \\subset B$ be an ideal with $IB \\subset J$.…",
  "detail": "Let $(A, I, \\gamma)$ be a divided power ring. Let $A \\to B$ be a ring map. Let $J \\subset B$ be an ideal with $IB \\subset J$. There exists a homomorphism of divided power rings $$ (A, I, \\gamma) \\longrightarrow (D, \\bar J, \\bar \\gamma) $$ such that $$ \\Hom_{(A, I, \\gamma)}((D, \\bar J, \\bar \\gamma), (C, K, \\delta)) = \\Hom_{(A, I)}((B, J), (C, K)) $$ functorially in the divided power algebra $(C, K, \\delta)$ over $(A, I, \\gamma)$. Here the LHS is morphisms of divided power rings over $(A, I, \\gamma)$ and the RHS is morphisms of (ring, ideal) pairs over $(A, I)$.",
