  "summary": "Let $(A, I, \\gamma)$ be a divided power ring. Let $M$ be an $A$-module. Let $B = A \\oplus M$ as an $A$-algebra where $M$ is an ideal of square zero and set $J =…",
  "detail": "Let $(A, I, \\gamma)$ be a divided power ring. Let $M$ be an $A$-module. Let $B = A \\oplus M$ as an $A$-algebra where $M$ is an ideal of square zero and set $J = I \\oplus M$. Set $$ \\delta_n(x + z) = \\gamma_n(x) + \\gamma_{n - 1}(x)z $$ for $x \\in I$ and $z \\in M$. Then $\\delta$ is a divided power structure and $A \\to B$ is a homomorphism of divided power rings from $(A, I, \\gamma)$ to $(B, J, \\delta)$.",
