  "importance": 0.54,
  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Let $(A, I, \\gamma) \\to (B, J, \\delta)$ be a homomorphism of divided power rings. Let $(B(1), J(1), \\delta(1))$ be the coproduct of $(B, J, \\delta)$ with itself…",
  "detail": "Let $(A, I, \\gamma) \\to (B, J, \\delta)$ be a homomorphism of divided power rings. Let $(B(1), J(1), \\delta(1))$ be the coproduct of $(B, J, \\delta)$ with itself over $(A, I, \\gamma)$, i.e., such that $$ \\xymatrix{ (B, J, \\delta) \\ar[r] & (B(1), J(1), \\delta(1)) \\\\ (A, I, \\gamma) \\ar[r] \\ar[u] & (B, J, \\delta) \\ar[u] } $$ is cocartesian. Denote $K = \\Ker(B(1) \\to B)$. Then $K \\cap J(1) \\subset J(1)$ is preserved by the divided power structure and $$ \\Omega_{B/A, \\delta} = K/ \\left(K^2 + (K \\cap J(1))^{[2]}\\right) $$ canonically.",
