  "summary": "Let $(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$ be a ringed space. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules. Let $I$ be a set.…",
  "detail": "Let $(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$ be a ringed space. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules. Let $I$ be a set. Let $s_i$, $i \\in I$ be a collection of local sections of $\\mathcal{F}$, i.e., $s_i \\in \\mathcal{F}(U_i)$ for some opens $U_i \\subset X$. There exists a unique smallest subsheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules $\\mathcal{G}$ such that each $s_i$ corresponds to a local section of $\\mathcal{G}$.",
  "source": "Stacks Project, lemma 01AP（modules.tex · Sections of sheaves of modules）"
