  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $R$ be a ring. Let $G$ be a finite group of order $n$ acting on $R$. Let $J \\subset R^G$ be an ideal.…",
  "detail": "Let $R$ be a ring. Let $G$ be a finite group of order $n$ acting on $R$. Let $J \\subset R^G$ be an ideal. Then $R^G/J \\to (R/JR)^G$ is ring map such that for $b \\in (R/JR)^G$ there is a monic polynomial $P \\in R^G/J[T]$ whose image in $(R/JR)^G[T]$ is $(T - b)^n$, for $a \\in \\Ker(R^G/J \\to (R/JR)^G)$ we have $(T - a)^n = T^n$ in $R^G/J[T]$. In particular, $R^G/J \\to (R/JR)^G$ is an integral ring map which induces homeomorphisms on spectra and purely inseparable extensions of residue fields.",
