  "family": "foundation",
  "summary": "Let $A$ be a ring which contains a primitive $p$th root of unity $\\zeta$. Set $w = 1 - \\zeta$.…",
  "detail": "Let $A$ be a ring which contains a primitive $p$th root of unity $\\zeta$. Set $w = 1 - \\zeta$. Then $$ P(z) = \\frac{(1 + wz)^p - 1}{w^p} = z^p - z + \\sum\\nolimits_{0 < i < p} a_i z^i $$ is an element of $A[z]$ and in fact $a_i \\in (w)$. Moreover, we have $$ P(z_1 + z_2 + w z_1 z_2) = P(z_1) + P(z_2) + w^p P(z_1) P(z_2) $$ in the polynomial ring $A[z_1, z_2]$.",
