  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $g : S' \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Denote $f' : X' \\to S'$ the base change of $f$ by $g$ and denote $g' : X' \\to X$ the projection. Assume $X$ is locally of finite type over $S$. Let $U \\subset X$ (resp.\\ $U' \\subset X'$) be the set of points where $f$ (resp.\\ $f'$) is quasi-finite. Then $U' = U \\times_S S' = (g')^{-1}(U)$. The base change of a locally quasi-finite morphism is locally quasi-finite. The base change of a quasi-finite morphism is quasi-finite.",
