  "detail": "Let $X$ be a scheme. There is a functor $$ \\det : \\left\\{ \\begin{matrix} \\text{category of perfect complexes} \\\\ \\text{with tor amplitude in }[-1, 0] \\\\ \\text{morphisms are isomorphisms} \\end{matrix} \\right\\} \\longrightarrow \\left\\{ \\begin{matrix} \\text{category of invertible modules} \\\\ \\text{morphisms are isomorphisms} \\end{matrix} \\right\\} $$ In addition, given a rank $0$ perfect object $L$ of $D(\\mathcal{O}_X)$ with tor-amplitude in $[-1, 0]$ there is a canonical element $\\delta(L) \\in \\Gamma(X, \\det(L))$ such that for any isomorphism $a : L \\to K$ in $D(\\mathcal{O}_X)$ we have $\\det(a)(\\delta(L)) = \\delta(K)$. Moreover, the construction is affine locally given by the construction of More on Algebra, Section \\ref{more-algebra-section-determinants-complexes}.",
