  "importance": 0.54,
  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $f$ is separated then for every pair of affine opens $(U, V)$ of $X$ which map into a common affine open of $S$ w…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $f$ is separated then for every pair of affine opens $(U, V)$ of $X$ which map into a common affine open of $S$ we have the intersection $U \\cap V$ is affine. the ring map $\\mathcal{O}_X(U) \\otimes_{\\mathbf{Z}} \\mathcal{O}_X(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U \\cap V)$ is surjective. If any pair of points $x_1, x_2 \\in X$ lying over a common point $s \\in S$ are contained in affine opens $x_1 \\in U$, $x_2 \\in V$ which map into a common affine open of $S$ such that (a), (b) hold, then $f$ is separated.",
