  "latex": "f_p\\mathcal{G}(U) = \\colim_{f(U) \\subset V} \\mathcal{G}(V)",
  "name": "lemma · Continuous maps and sheaves",
  "en": "lemma-pullback-presheaves",
  "importance": 0.54,
  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a continuous map. There exists a functor $f_p : \\textit{PSh}(Y) \\to \\textit{PSh}(X)$ which is left adjoint to $f_*$.…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a continuous map. There exists a functor $f_p : \\textit{PSh}(Y) \\to \\textit{PSh}(X)$ which is left adjoint to $f_*$. For a presheaf $\\mathcal{G}$ it is determined by the rule $$ f_p\\mathcal{G}(U) = \\colim_{f(U) \\subset V} \\mathcal{G}(V) $$ where the colimit is over the collection of open neighbourhoods $V$ of $f(U)$ in $Y$. The colimits are over directed partially ordered sets. (The restriction mappings of $f_p\\mathcal{G}$ are explained in the proof.)",
