  "url": "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B2F",
  "env": "lemma",
  "latex": "\\text{d}f : T_{X/S, x} \\longrightarrow T_{Y/S, y}",
  "name": "lemma · Tangent spaces",
  "en": "lemma-map-tangent-spaces",
  "importance": 0.54,
  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes over a base scheme $S$. Let $x \\in X$ be a point. Set $y = f(x)$.…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes over a base scheme $S$. Let $x \\in X$ be a point. Set $y = f(x)$. If $\\kappa(y) = \\kappa(x)$, then $f$ induces a natural linear map $$ \\text{d}f : T_{X/S, x} \\longrightarrow T_{Y/S, y} $$ which is dual to the linear map $\\Omega_{Y/S, y} \\otimes \\kappa(y) \\to \\Omega_{X/S, x} \\otimes \\kappa(x)$ via the identifications of Lemma \\ref{lemma-tangent-space-cotangent-space}.",
