  "latex": "H^n(X \\times_{\\Spec(k)} Y, \\text{pr}_1^*\\mathcal{F} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_{X \\times_{\\Spec(k)} Y}} \\text{pr}_2^*\\mathcal{G}) = \\bigoplus\\nolimits_{p + q = n} H^p(X, \\mathcal{F}) \\otimes_k H^q(Y, \\mathcal{G})",
  "name": "lemma · K\\\"unneth formula, I",
  "en": "lemma-kunneth-general",
  "importance": 0.54,
  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes over $k$ and let $\\mathcal{F}$, resp.\\ $\\mathcal{G}$ be a quasi-coherent $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module, resp.\\ $\\mathcal…",
  "detail": "Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes over $k$ and let $\\mathcal{F}$, resp.\\ $\\mathcal{G}$ be a quasi-coherent $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module, resp.\\ $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-module. Then we have a canonical isomorphism $$ H^n(X \\times_{\\Spec(k)} Y, \\text{pr}_1^*\\mathcal{F} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_{X \\times_{\\Spec(k)} Y}} \\text{pr}_2^*\\mathcal{G}) = \\bigoplus\\nolimits_{p + q = n} H^p(X, \\mathcal{F}) \\otimes_k H^q(Y, \\mathcal{G}) $$ provided $X$ and $Y$ are quasi-compact and quasi-separated.",
