  "family": "curve",
  "summary": "Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $D \\subset S$ be an effective Cartier divisor with ideal sheaf $\\mathcal{I}_D$.…",
  "detail": "Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $D \\subset S$ be an effective Cartier divisor with ideal sheaf $\\mathcal{I}_D$. The {\\it invertible sheaf $\\mathcal{O}_S(D)$ associated to $D$} is defined by $$ \\mathcal{O}_S(D) = \\SheafHom_{\\mathcal{O}_S}(\\mathcal{I}_D, \\mathcal{O}_S) = \\mathcal{I}_D^{\\otimes -1}. $$ The {\\it canonical section}, usually denoted $1$ or $1_D$, is the global section of $\\mathcal{O}_S(D)$ corresponding to the inclusion mapping $\\mathcal{I}_D \\to \\mathcal{O}_S$. We write $\\mathcal{O}_S(-D) = \\mathcal{O}_S(D)^{\\otimes -1} = \\mathcal{I}_D$. Given a second effective Cartier divisor $D' \\subset S$ we define $\\mathcal{O}_S(D - D') = \\mathcal{O}_S(D) \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_S} \\mathcal{O}_S(-D')$.",
