  "importance": 0.49,
  "family": "curve",
  "summary": "Let $i : Z \\to X$ be an immersion of schemes. Choose an open subscheme $U \\subset X$ such that $i$ identifies $Z$ with a closed subscheme of $U$ and denote $\\ma…",
  "detail": "Let $i : Z \\to X$ be an immersion of schemes. Choose an open subscheme $U \\subset X$ such that $i$ identifies $Z$ with a closed subscheme of $U$ and denote $\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_U$ the corresponding quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. We say $i$ is a {\\it regular immersion} if $\\mathcal{I}$ is regular. We say $i$ is a {\\it Koszul-regular immersion} if $\\mathcal{I}$ is Koszul-regular. We say $i$ is a {\\it $H_1$-regular immersion} if $\\mathcal{I}$ is $H_1$-regular. We say $i$ is a {\\it quasi-regular immersion} if $\\mathcal{I}$ is quasi-regular.",
