  "family": "birational",
  "summary": "Let $R \\to S$ be a finite type ring map. Let $\\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $S$ lying over the prime $\\mathfrak r$ of $R$. Let $N$ be a finite $S$-module.…",
  "detail": "Let $R \\to S$ be a finite type ring map. Let $\\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $S$ lying over the prime $\\mathfrak r$ of $R$. Let $N$ be a finite $S$-module. A {\\it complete d\\'evissage of $N/S/R$ at $\\mathfrak q$} is given by a complete d\\'evissage $(A_i, B_i, M_i, \\alpha_i)_{i = 1, \\ldots, n}$ of $N/S/R$ over $\\mathfrak r$ and prime ideals $\\mathfrak q_i \\subset B_i$ lying over $\\mathfrak r$ such that $\\kappa(\\mathfrak r) \\subset \\kappa(\\mathfrak q_i)$ is purely transcendental, there is a unique prime $\\mathfrak q'_i \\subset A_i$ lying over $\\mathfrak q_i \\subset B_i$, $\\mathfrak q = \\mathfrak q'_1 \\cap S$ and $\\mathfrak q_i = \\mathfrak q'_{i + 1} \\cap A_i$, $R \\to B_i$ has relative dimension $\\dim_{\\mathfrak q_i}(\\text{Supp}(M_i \\otimes_R \\kappa(\\mathfrak r)))$.",
