  "en": "definition-proper-intersection",
  "importance": 0.49,
  "family": "intersect",
  "summary": "Let $X$ be a nonsingular variety. Let $W,V \\subset X$ be closed subvarieties with $\\dim(W) = s$ and $\\dim(V) = r$.…",
  "detail": "Let $X$ be a nonsingular variety. Let $W,V \\subset X$ be closed subvarieties with $\\dim(W) = s$ and $\\dim(V) = r$. We say that $W$ and $V$ {\\it intersect properly} if $\\dim(V \\cap W) \\leq r + s - \\dim(X)$. Let $\\alpha = \\sum n_i [W_i]$ be an $s$-cycle, and $\\beta = \\sum_j m_j [V_j]$ be an $r$-cycle on $X$. We say that $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ {\\it intersect properly} if $W_i$ and $V_j$ intersect properly for all $i$ and $j$.",
