  "detail": "Given morphisms of schemes $f : X \\to S$ and $g : Y \\to S$ the {\\it fibre product} is a scheme $X \\times_S Y$ together with projection morphisms $p : X \\times_S Y \\to X$ and $q : X \\times_S Y \\to Y$ sitting into the following commutative diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ X \\times_S Y \\ar[r]_q \\ar[d]_p & Y \\ar[d]^g \\\\ X \\ar[r]^f & S } $$ which is universal among all diagrams of this sort, see Categories, Definition \\ref{categories-definition-fibre-products}.",
