  "en": "definition-fibre",
  "importance": 0.49,
  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $s \\in S$ be a point. The {\\it scheme theoretic fibre $X_s$ of $f$ over $s$}, or simply the {\\it fibre of $f$ ov…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $s \\in S$ be a point. The {\\it scheme theoretic fibre $X_s$ of $f$ over $s$}, or simply the {\\it fibre of $f$ over $s$}, is the scheme fitting in the following fibre product diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ X_s = \\Spec(\\kappa(s)) \\times_S X \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\ar[d] \\\\ \\Spec(\\kappa(s)) \\ar[r] & S } $$ We think of the fibre $X_s$ always as a scheme over $\\kappa(s)$.",
  "source": "Stacks Project, definition 01K0（schemes.tex · Base change in algebraic geometry）"
