  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. We say $f$ is {\\it separated} if the diagonal morphism $\\Delta_{X/S}$ is a closed immersion.…",
  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes. We say $f$ is {\\it separated} if the diagonal morphism $\\Delta_{X/S}$ is a closed immersion. We say $f$ is {\\it quasi-separated} if the diagonal morphism $\\Delta_{X/S}$ is a quasi-compact morphism. We say a scheme $Y$ is {\\it separated} if the morphism $Y \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$ is separated. We say a scheme $Y$ is {\\it quasi-separated} if the morphism $Y \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$ is quasi-separated.",
