  "importance": 0.49,
  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $X$ be a topological space. A {\\it presheaf of abelian groups on $X$} or an {\\it abelian presheaf over $X$} is a presheaf of sets $\\mathcal{F}$ such that fo…",
  "detail": "Let $X$ be a topological space. A {\\it presheaf of abelian groups on $X$} or an {\\it abelian presheaf over $X$} is a presheaf of sets $\\mathcal{F}$ such that for each open $U \\subset X$ the set $\\mathcal{F}(U)$ is endowed with the structure of an abelian group, and such that all restriction maps $\\rho^U_V$ are homomorphisms of abelian groups, see Lemma \\ref{lemma-abelian-presheaves} above. A {\\it morphism of abelian presheaves over $X$} $\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$ is a morphism of presheaves of sets which induces a homomorphism of abelian groups $\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{G}(U)$ for every open $U \\subset X$. The category of presheaves of abelian groups on $X$ is denoted $\\textit{PAb}(X)$.",
