  "importance": 0.48,
  "family": "intersect",
  "summary": "Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $x \\in R$. If $M$ is a finite Cohen-Macaulay module over $R$ with $\\dim(\\text{Supp}(M)) = 1$ and $\\dim(\\text{Supp}(M/xM)…",
  "detail": "Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $x \\in R$. If $M$ is a finite Cohen-Macaulay module over $R$ with $\\dim(\\text{Supp}(M)) = 1$ and $\\dim(\\text{Supp}(M/xM)) = 0$, then $$ \\text{length}_R(M/xM) = \\sum\\nolimits_i \\text{length}_R(R/(x, \\mathfrak q_i)) \\text{length}_{R_{\\mathfrak q_i}}(M_{\\mathfrak q_i}). $$ where $\\mathfrak q_1, \\ldots, \\mathfrak q_t$ are the minimal primes of the support of $M$. If $I \\subset R$ is an ideal such that $x$ is a nonzerodivisor on $R/I$ and $\\dim(R/I) = 1$, then $$ \\text{length}_R(R/(x, I)) = \\sum\\nolimits_i \\text{length}_R(R/(x, \\mathfrak q_i)) \\text{length}_{R_{\\mathfrak q_i}}((R/I)_{\\mathfrak q_i}) $$ where $\\mathfrak q_1, \\ldots, \\mathfrak q_n$ are the minimal primes over $I$.",
