  "detail": "Let $(S, \\delta)$ be as in Situation \\ref{situation-setup}. Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a proper morphism of schemes which are locally of finite type over $S$. Let $Z \\subset X$ be a closed subscheme with $\\dim_\\delta(Z) \\leq k$. Then $$ f_*[Z]_k = [f_*{\\mathcal O}_Z]_k. $$ Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent sheaf on $X$ such that $\\dim_\\delta(\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F})) \\leq k$. Then $$ f_*[\\mathcal{F}]_k = [f_*{\\mathcal F}]_k. $$ Note that the statement makes sense since $f_*\\mathcal{F}$ and $f_*\\mathcal{O}_Z$ are coherent $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-modules by Cohomology of Schemes, Proposition \\ref{coherent-proposition-proper-pushforward-coherent}.",
