  "summary": "Let $K$ be any field. Let $X$ be a $1$-dimensional integral scheme endowed with a proper morphism $c : X \\to \\Spec(K)$.…",
  "detail": "Let $K$ be any field. Let $X$ be a $1$-dimensional integral scheme endowed with a proper morphism $c : X \\to \\Spec(K)$. Let $f \\in K(X)^*$ be an invertible rational function. Then $$ \\sum\\nolimits_{x \\in X \\text{ closed}} [\\kappa(x) : K] \\text{ord}_{\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}}(f) = 0 $$ where $\\text{ord}$ is as in Algebra, Definition \\ref{algebra-definition-ord}. In other words, $c_*\\text{div}(f) = 0$.",
