  "detail": "Let $(S, \\delta)$ be as in Situation \\ref{situation-setup}. Let $X$, $Y$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a proper morphism. Let $\\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible sheaf on $Y$. Let $s$ be a nonzero meromorphic section $s$ of $\\mathcal{L}$ on $Y$. Assume $X$, $Y$ integral, $f$ dominant, and $\\dim_\\delta(X) = \\dim_\\delta(Y)$. Then $$ f_*\\left(\\text{div}_{f^*\\mathcal{L}}(f^*s)\\right) = [R(X) : R(Y)]\\text{div}_\\mathcal{L}(s). $$ as cycles on $Y$. In particular $$ f_*(c_1(f^*\\mathcal{L}) \\cap [X]) = [R(X) : R(Y)] c_1(\\mathcal{L}) \\cap [Y] = c_1(\\mathcal{L}) \\cap f_*[X] $$",
