  "summary": "Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let $X$ be a smooth projective curve of genus $g$ over $k$.…",
  "detail": "Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let $X$ be a smooth projective curve of genus $g$ over $k$. If $n \\geq 1$ is invertible in $k$, then $\\Pic(X)[n] \\cong (\\mathbf{Z}/n\\mathbf{Z})^{\\oplus 2g}$. If the characteristic of $k$ is $p > 0$, then there exists an integer $0 \\leq f \\leq g$ such that $\\Pic(X)[p^m] \\cong (\\mathbf{Z}/p^m\\mathbf{Z})^{\\oplus f}$ for all $m \\geq 1$.",
