  "family": "curve",
  "summary": "In Situation \\ref{situation-Cohen-Macaulay-curve} assume $X$ is integral and has genus $g$. Let $\\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module.…",
  "detail": "In Situation \\ref{situation-Cohen-Macaulay-curve} assume $X$ is integral and has genus $g$. Let $\\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module. Let $Z \\subset X$ be a $0$-dimensional closed subscheme with ideal sheaf $\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_X$. If $H^1(X, \\mathcal{I}\\mathcal{L})$ is nonzero, then $$ \\deg(\\mathcal{L}) \\leq 2g - 2 + \\deg(Z) $$ with strict inequality unless $\\mathcal{I}\\mathcal{L} \\cong \\omega_X$.",
