  "summary": "Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper scheme over $k$ of dimension $1$ with $H^0(X, \\mathcal{O}_X) = k$. Assume the singularities of $X$ are at-worst-nodal.…",
  "detail": "Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper scheme over $k$ of dimension $1$ with $H^0(X, \\mathcal{O}_X) = k$. Assume the singularities of $X$ are at-worst-nodal. Consider a sequence $$ X = X_0 \\to X_1 \\to \\ldots \\to X_n = X' $$ of contractions of rational tails (Example \\ref{example-rational-tail}) until none are left. Then if the genus of $X$ is $0$, then $X'$ is an irreducible plane conic, if the genus of $X$ is $1$, then $\\omega_{X'} \\cong \\mathcal{O}_X$, if the genus of $X$ is $> 1$, then $\\omega_{X'}^{\\otimes m}$ is globally generated for $m \\geq 2$. If the genus of $X$ is $\\geq 1$, then the morphism $X \\to X'$ is independent of choices and formation of this morphism commutes with base field extensions.",
