  "importance": 0.48,
  "family": "curve",
  "summary": "Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let $X$ be an at-worst-nodal, proper, connected $1$-dimensional scheme over $k$.…",
  "detail": "Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let $X$ be an at-worst-nodal, proper, connected $1$-dimensional scheme over $k$. Let $\\nu : X^\\nu \\to X$ be the normalization. Let $S \\subset X^\\nu$ be the set of points where $\\nu$ is not an isomorphism. Then $$ \\text{Der}_k(\\mathcal{O}_X, \\mathcal{O}_X) = \\{D' \\in \\text{Der}_k(\\mathcal{O}_{X^\\nu}, \\mathcal{O}_{X^\\nu}) \\mid D' \\text{ fixes every }x^\\nu \\in S\\} $$",
  "source": "Stacks Project, lemma 0E68（curves.tex · Vector fields）"
