  "summary": "Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent sheaf on $X$.…",
  "detail": "Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent sheaf on $X$. The set of coherent subsheaves $$ \\{ \\mathcal{K} \\subset \\mathcal{F} \\mid \\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{K})\\text{ is nowhere dense in }\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F}) \\} $$ has a maximal element $\\mathcal{K}$. Setting $\\mathcal{F}' = \\mathcal{F}/\\mathcal{K}$ we have the following $\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F}') = \\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F})$, $\\mathcal{F}'$ has no embedded associated points, and there exists a dense open $U \\subset X$ such that $U \\cap \\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F})$ is dense in $\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F})$ and $\\mathcal{F}'|_U \\cong \\mathcal{F}|_U$.",
