  "importance": 0.48,
  "family": "curve",
  "summary": "Let $Z \\subset X$ be a closed subscheme of a Noetherian scheme. Assume $Z$ has no embedded points, every irreducible component of $Z$ has codimension $1$ in $X$…",
  "detail": "Let $Z \\subset X$ be a closed subscheme of a Noetherian scheme. Assume $Z$ has no embedded points, every irreducible component of $Z$ has codimension $1$ in $X$, every local ring $\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$, $x \\in Z$ is a UFD or $X$ is regular. Then $Z$ is an effective Cartier divisor.",
