  "summary": "Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\\mathcal{J}$ be a sheaf of ideals. Then $\\mathcal{J}$ is regular (resp.\\ Koszul-regular, $H_1$-regular, quasi-regular) if and only if …",
  "detail": "Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\\mathcal{J}$ be a sheaf of ideals. Then $\\mathcal{J}$ is regular (resp.\\ Koszul-regular, $H_1$-regular, quasi-regular) if and only if for every $x \\in \\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{O}_X/\\mathcal{J})$ there exists an affine open neighbourhood $x \\in U \\subset X$, $U = \\Spec(A)$ such that $\\mathcal{J}|_U = \\widetilde{I}$ and such that $I$ is generated by a regular (resp.\\ Koszul-regular, $H_1$-regular, quasi-regular) sequence $f_1, \\ldots, f_r \\in A$.",
