  "detail": "Let $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of locally ringed spaces. Assume that pullbacks of meromorphic functions are defined for $f$ (see Definition \\ref{definition-pullback-meromorphic-sections}). Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-modules. There is a canonical pullback map $f^* : \\Gamma(Y, \\mathcal{K}_Y(\\mathcal{F})) \\to \\Gamma(X, \\mathcal{K}_X(f^*\\mathcal{F}))$ for meromorphic sections of $\\mathcal{F}$. Let $\\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-module. A regular meromorphic section $s$ of $\\mathcal{L}$ pulls back to a regular meromorphic section $f^*s$ of $f^*\\mathcal{L}$.",
