  "summary": "Let $b : X' \\to X$ be the blowing up of the scheme $X$ along a closed subscheme $Z$.…",
  "detail": "Let $b : X' \\to X$ be the blowing up of the scheme $X$ along a closed subscheme $Z$. Let $U = \\Spec(A)$ be an affine open of $X$ and let $I \\subset A$ be the ideal corresponding to $Z \\cap U$. Let $a \\in I$ and let $x' \\in X'$ be a point mapping to a point of $U$. Then $x'$ is a point of the affine open $U' = \\Spec(A[\\frac{I}{a}])$ if and only if the image of $a$ in $\\mathcal{O}_{X', x'}$ cuts out the exceptional divisor.",
