  "url": "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01IB",
  "env": "lemma",
  "latex": "(X, \\mathcal{O}_X) = (\\Spec(R), \\mathcal{O}_{\\Spec(R)})",
  "name": "lemma · Quasi-coherent sheaves on affines",
  "en": "lemma-equivalence-quasi-coherent",
  "importance": 0.48,
  "family": "scheme",
  "summary": "Let $(X, \\mathcal{O}_X) = (\\Spec(R), \\mathcal{O}_{\\Spec(R)})$ be an affine scheme.…",
  "detail": "Let $(X, \\mathcal{O}_X) = (\\Spec(R), \\mathcal{O}_{\\Spec(R)})$ be an affine scheme. The functors $M \\mapsto \\widetilde M$ and $\\mathcal{F} \\mapsto \\Gamma(X, \\mathcal{F})$ define quasi-inverse equivalences of categories $$ \\xymatrix{ \\QCoh(\\mathcal{O}_X) \\ar@<1ex>[r] & \\text{Mod}_R \\ar@<1ex>[l] } $$ between the category of quasi-coherent $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules and the category of $R$-modules.",
