  "detail": "Let $k_1, \\ldots, k_n$ be fields. For any monomorphism of schemes $X \\to \\Spec(k_1 \\times \\ldots \\times k_n)$ there exists a subset $I \\subset \\{1, \\ldots, n\\}$ such that $X \\cong \\Spec(\\prod_{i \\in I} k_i)$ as schemes over $\\Spec(k_1 \\times \\ldots \\times k_n)$. More generally, if $X = \\coprod_{i \\in I} \\Spec(k_i)$ is a disjoint union of spectra of fields and $Y \\to X$ is a monomorphism, then there exists a subset $J \\subset I$ such that $Y = \\coprod_{i \\in J} \\Spec(k_i)$.",
