  "detail": "With $X$, $\\mathcal{O}_1$, $\\mathcal{O}_2$, $\\mathcal{F}$ and $\\mathcal{G}$ as above there exists a canonical bijection $$ \\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_1}(\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}_{\\mathcal{O}_1}) = \\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_2}( \\mathcal{O}_2 \\otimes_{p, \\mathcal{O}_1} \\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F} ) $$ In other words, the restriction and change of rings functors are adjoint to each other.",
