  "summary": "Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf of abelian groups on $X$.…",
  "detail": "Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf of abelian groups on $X$. There exists a unique structure of an abelian group on $\\mathcal{F}_x$ such that for every $U \\subset X$ open, $x\\in U$ the map $\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}_x$ is a group homomorphism. Moreover, $$ \\mathcal{F}_x = \\colim_{x\\in U} \\mathcal{F}(U) $$ holds in the category of abelian groups.",
