  "summary": "Let $(f, f^\\sharp) : (X, \\mathcal{O}_X) \\to (Y, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules.…",
  "detail": "Let $(f, f^\\sharp) : (X, \\mathcal{O}_X) \\to (Y, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules. Let $\\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of $\\mathcal{O}_Y$-modules. There is a canonical bijection $$ \\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(f^*\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}) = \\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_Y}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}). $$ In other words: the functor $f^*$ is the left adjoint to $f_*$.",
