  "detail": "Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper scheme over $k$. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module. Let $\\mathcal{L}_1, \\ldots, \\mathcal{L}_r$ be invertible $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules. Let $d = \\dim(\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F}))$. Let $Z_i \\subset X$ be the irreducible components of $\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F})$ of dimension $d$. Let $\\xi_i \\in Z_i$ be the generic point and set $m_i = \\text{length}_{\\mathcal{O}_{X, \\xi_i}}(\\mathcal{F}_{\\xi_i})$. Then $$ \\chi(X, \\mathcal{F} \\otimes \\mathcal{L}_1^{\\otimes n_1} \\otimes \\ldots \\otimes \\mathcal{L}_r^{\\otimes n_r}) - \\sum\\nolimits_i m_i\\ \\chi(Z_i, \\mathcal{L}_1^{\\otimes n_1} \\otimes \\ldots \\otimes \\mathcal{L}_r^{\\otimes n_r}|_{Z_i}) $$ is a numerical polynomial in $n_1, \\ldots, n_r$ of total degree $< d$.",
