  "summary": "Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a category with products. A presheaf $\\mathcal{F}$ with values in $\\mathcal{C}$ on $X$ is a {\\it sheaf} if …",
  "detail": "Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a category with products. A presheaf $\\mathcal{F}$ with values in $\\mathcal{C}$ on $X$ is a {\\it sheaf} if for every open covering the diagram $$ \\xymatrix{ \\mathcal{F}(U) \\ar[r] & \\prod\\nolimits_{i\\in I} \\mathcal{F}(U_i) \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] & \\prod\\nolimits_{(i_0, i_1) \\in I \\times I} \\mathcal{F}(U_{i_0} \\cap U_{i_1}) } $$ is an equalizer diagram in the category $\\mathcal{C}$.",
