  "summary": "Let $X$ be a scheme over the field $k$. Let $x \\in X$. We say $X$ is {\\it geometrically normal at $x$} if for every field extension $k'/k$ and every $x' \\in X_{…",
  "detail": "Let $X$ be a scheme over the field $k$. Let $x \\in X$. We say $X$ is {\\it geometrically normal at $x$} if for every field extension $k'/k$ and every $x' \\in X_{k'}$ lying over $x$ the local ring $\\mathcal{O}_{X_{k'}, x'}$ is normal. We say $X$ is {\\it geometrically normal} over $k$ if $X$ is geometrically normal at every $x \\in X$.",
